          "prompt": "MANDATORY: ONE SINGLE HORIZONTAL ROW of exactly four separate orthographic views of the SAME object, left to right: 1 FRONT view; 2 LEFT side view (object turned so its front points to the LEFT edge of the image); 3 BACK view; 4 RIGHT side view (object turned so its front points to the RIGHT edge of the image). Same scale and same ground line in all four, wide empty gaps between the views, every view complete and not cropped. Plain flat light neutral grey background (#D6D6D6). No floor, no ground shadow, no text, no labels, no frames, no perspective, no extra objects. No fire, no smoke, no sparks, no lava stream, no lava pool, no glow halo: hot cracks and furnace interiors are painted only as flat opaque bright orange-yellow colour areas. STYLE: stylized hand-painted 3D game environment asset in the readable style of Gunfire Reborn: bold chunky silhouette, broad clean faceted planes, two or three dominant colour blocks (dark charcoal basalt, black iron with big rivets, deep vermilion lacquer, warm dark bronze), soft painted gradients, sparse wear, soot-darkened edges. No photorealism, no micro-grain, no dense tiny cracks, no tiny carvings, no harsh highlights. OBJECT (12m wide x 10m tall x 8m deep): A sturdy two-level work scaffold built against a rock wall, made of thick black iron posts and girders with big rivets and heavy charred dark timber beams and planks. LOWER LEVEL: a FLAT plank deck 4.5m above the ground covering the LEFT half. UPPER LEVEL: a FLAT plank deck 9m above the ground covering the whole width at the top. One straight wide black iron ramp with cleats, 3m wide, climbs at a gentle slope across the FRONT face from the lower deck on the LEFT up to the upper deck at the RIGHT. Both decks have a simple black iron railing 1.1m tall on their open edges with vermilion lacquered post caps. The BACK of the scaffold is a FLAT vertical face with no railing (it is set against the rock wall). Thick chunky members only, every post at least 0.5m thick. PROPORTIONS: FRONT and BACK views about 1.2 times as wide as tall; LEFT and RIGHT views about 0.8 times as wide as tall.",
